# 10. Conditions for Falsification

The conjecture would be falsified if:

1. Proton structure is conclusively shown to be incompatible with tetrahedral geometry.
2. No geometric interpretation of the proton radii remains viable.
3. Experimental evidence demonstrates continuous sub-femtometre contraction of electromagnetic quanta.
4. The proposed gauge relations produce contradictions with established electromagnetic conservation laws.
5. The framework fails to generate any experimentally distinguishable predictions from standard quantum field theory.

